# 3D visualization / simulation auxiliary layers (500+) for interconnect bodies.
#
# Post-passivation physical volumes for 3D rendering, EM simulation, and
# thermal analysis. NOT fabrication layers. Owned by the interconnect PDK
# (split out of the interposer PDK layers_def.drc:136-151). Geometry is
# generated by interconnect_pdk/libs.tech/klayout/python/bump3d_generator.py
# and the hyp_to_gds converter.
#
# Layer numbers 500+ chosen to avoid collision with IHP SG13G2 upstream
# layers (<200). Datatype convention: 35 = pillar, 36 = sbump.

# --- IHP PacTech Cu pillar / solder bump ---
#   CuPillar  (500/35): Cu body, 28-42 um height, 44-54 um diameter (Table 6.1)
#   SnAgCap   (501/35): SnAg solder cap, 16-19 um height (Table 6.1)
#   SolderBall(502/36): SAC305 ball, 80 um diameter (Section 6.9.1)
cupillar_body = polygons(500, 35)
snag_cap      = polygons(501, 35)
solder_ball   = polygons(502, 36)

# --- VendorX fine-pitch microbump (DEMO, non-IHP) ---
#   VendorXBumpCu  (510/35): Cu post, 18 um height, 40 um diameter
#   VendorXBumpCap (511/35): SnAg cap, 6 um height
vendorx_bump_cu  = polygons(510, 35)
vendorx_bump_cap = polygons(511, 35)
